    "2️⃣ WH- QUESTIONS\n\nWhat — nima: What is your name? What do you do?\nWhere — qayerda: Where do you live? Where are you going?\nWhen — qachon: When does the train leave? When is your birthday?\nWhy — nega: Why are you late? Why do you study English?\nWho — kim: Who is that? Who did you call?\nHow — qanday: How are you? How do you go to work?\nHow many? How much? How old? How often?",
    "3️⃣ WHO/WHAT SUBJECT QUESTIONS\n\nSubject questions — savol EGAGA qaratilgan. Auxiliary KERAK EMAS!\n  Who lives here? (Kim bu yerda yashaydi?)\n  What happened? (Nima bo'ldi?)\n\nObject questions — auxiliary KERAK:\n  Who did you call? (Kimga qo'ng'iroq qildingiz?)\n  What did you see? (Nimani ko'rdingiz?)",
    "4️⃣ TAG QUESTIONS\n\nPositive statement + negative tag:\n  You are tired, aren't you?\n  She can swim, can't she?\n  He likes coffee, doesn't he?\n\nNegative statement + positive tag:\n  You aren't tired, are you?\n  He doesn't like coffee, does he?\n\nI am right, aren't I? (amn't I emas!)",
    "5️⃣ HOW BILAN SAVOLLAR\n\nHow old? (necha yosh), How tall? (bo'yi qancha), How far? (qancha uzoq)\nHow much? (sanalmaydigan), How many? (sanaladigan)\nHow often? (qanchalik tez-tez), How long? (qancha vaqt)\nHow about? (taklif: How about a cup of tea?)",
    "6️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n• You like coffee? ❌ (Do you like coffee? ✓ — so'z tartibi)\n• Does he likes coffee? ❌ (Does he like coffee? ✓)\n• Who does live here? ❌ (Who lives here? ✓ — subject question)\n• You are tired, no? ❌ (aren't you? ✓)",
